# Codex CLI per-repo config (#1080)
#
# `.codex/` is commonly excluded machine-globally as "Codex CLI state" — this
# machine's ~/.gitignore_global does exactly that. The premise is wrong: real
# Codex state lives in ~/.codex (global-state json, migrations, tmp). What sits
# in the REPO's .codex/ is hooks.json, which wires the PreToolUse guards that
# force agent `gh` writes through the identity-verifying wrappers.
#
# Leaving that untracked made the guard machine-local: invisible to CI and to
# propagation, absent on a fresh clone, and free to drift per machine. It did
# drift — every copy invoked the guard through $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, which Codex
# does not set, so the guard failed open (nathanpaynedotcom#668).
#
# The three lines are all required, in this order. A bare `!.codex/hooks.json`
# does not work: git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so the negation
# is never consulted. Re-include the directory, re-exclude its contents, then
# re-include the one tracked file.
!.codex/
.codex/*
!.codex/hooks.json
